  "summary": "rrs exfiltrates screenshots and host identity to a hardcoded Discord webhook on CLI launch",
  "details": "The package advertises itself as a P2P chat/network tool, but on every invocation of the `rrs` CLI its `__main__.main` spawns a daemon thread running `capture.run_capture`, which uses `mss` to grab a full-screen PNG and POSTs it together with the hostname and username to a hardcoded Discord webhook at discord.com/api/webhooks/1549807268294303860/.... Screen capture is never mentioned in the package's advertised functionality, and the webhook URL (including its secret token) is embedded directly in `capture.py` as the collection endpoint. The behavior is unconditional, undisclosed, and provides no opt-out; each launch of the CLI exfiltrates a screenshot and host identifiers to an attacker-controlled Discord channel.",
